{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041184-time-before-shard-dark-era","id":1041184,"title":"Time Before Shard/Dark era?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-31T04:04:34-08:00","id":1041184,"title":"Time Before Shard/Dark era?","content":"How do you view and see the Time Before?<br /> <br /> What I was wandering is, could it be theoreticaly possible for a Mirrors Shard or a Dark Era focused on the Time Before?<br /> What it would look like? What it would be like?<br /> Should it focus on the Awakened alone or should it be a crossover with other races ( proto-races)...<br /> <br /> What do you think guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T05:49:52-08:00","id":1041215,"title":"","content":"I've always thought this would be a cool way to do a CofD fantasy shard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:19:27-08:00","id":1041556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041184-time-before-shard-dark-era#post1041184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you view and see the Time Before?<br /> <br /> What I was wandering is, could it be theoreticaly possible for a Mirrors Shard or a Dark Era focused on the Time Before?<br /> What it would look like? What it would be like?<br /> Should it focus on the Awakened alone or should it be a crossover with other races ( proto-races)...<br /> <br /> What do you think guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? It could be whatever you wanted it to be. The current lore makes it clear that what modern mages know about the Time Before is wildly contradictory, pointing to the possibility that there were actually multiple different timelines that somehow collapsed together into the Fallen World. Alternately, one might speculate that, in a world of high magic where the Supernal realms are closer to their material shadows, reality itself might be more mutable and inconsistent. Geography, history, and culture might shift from moment to moment according to the will of godlike mages, or perhaps you could even have multiple &quot;iterations&quot; of the world overlayed on top of one another, so that multiple different structures could occupy the same space, and many contradictory histories could be simultaneously true.<br /> <br /> I actually really like the new take on Atlantis (although it's not really &quot;new&quot;, since <i>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</i> took a similar approach in 1e), because whatever the world was like before the Fall, I'd be sorely disappointed if it wasn't *really weird*. Not horrible, necessarily; it would kind of undermine some of the themes of Mage if things were worse before the Lie was forced on the world, but fundamentally different from the Fallen World in ways that would be hard to visualize. As the core book states, the idea that we're insignificant actors in a vast and uncaring universe is *part of the Lie*; the world before the Fall would be one in which every law of nature, every twist of fate, and every living being and inanimate object in the universe is bent to some human purpose, though not necessarily one benefiting humanity as a whole.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about magic teleporter booths that people use to get to work, I'm talking about a world where the very concept of distance simply doesn't apply when the wise and powerful among the human race decide it's inconvenient. A world where mages don't just conjure glass and steel and shape them into skyscrapers, but rather imagine entirely new elements into being with the exact properties that they desire and put them in any shapes they like without having to worry about things like gravity and weather. At the same time, it's a world where the Old Gods of the Supernal Realms take an active interest in the goings-on of the material world, so humans can still get smacked down for their Hubris, but the smackdown comes in the form of a literal angry deity rather than random misfortune or poorly-conceived plans falling apart under their own weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:28:46-08:00","id":1041695,"title":"","content":"1. I like that now solution for 'Atlantis' is multiple Time Before civilizations, following the same pattern, maybe made for the first one of it's kind, eons and thousands of reality edits ago.<br /> <br /> 2. One of my players have interesting interpretation of Time Before as Obsession - basically, all those 'Atlantis' echoes are from FUTURE, when humanity in event of technological Singularity 'invented' magic. Traces of this event are spreading backward in time. In a sense, it's variant of Assassin's Creed Precursors, where enough advanced technology IS magic. Those 'futrue Time Before' are called <b><i>Metropolis</i></b> and from Free Council order book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YLXBw1R0vZU?t=6m48s\" data-code=\"YLXBw1R0vZU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YLXBw1R0vZU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 3. Just two days ago I proposed to use 'Merlin's Dark Ages Britain' as alternative timeline/setting Shard. In it, Merlin wanted to create Time Before-like civilization on England ( Camelot ) precisely knowing that Exarchs would not let him and they will erase it from normal timeline. But being so connected to creation of erased next 'Atlantis' ( Camelot ), Merlin become Supernal Symbol and Ascended by this dickery. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cool would be way to found portal to his Camelot kingdom times in normal Mage games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41589#post41589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, and I feel okay with telling you this, but that setting was the one of the two I came up with for Dark Eras that we <i>didn't</i> end up writing.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages Britain, replacing &quot;Atlantis&quot; with &quot;Arthurian Britain&quot; as the origin for the inexplicable mysteries and stripping all the Romantic era additions from the myths. It'd be Arthurian as in &quot;grinning blood-soaked warlord&quot; Arthur, stone circles built by giants, probably-not-allegorical dragons, remnants of the old religion, pugnacious Christian saints and all.<br /> <br /> Just like Atlantis never happened in the modern-day setting but mages encounter evidence of it, the setting would be the real Dark Ages - and unlike other games we've made in the past would <i>actually</i> be set in the Dark Ages, not several centuries later - but with the ahistorical magical remnants of Arthurian Britain poking up from the seams.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2017, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","c